.\" Adapted from ~/stow/zephyr/man/zephyr.1; checked against Aether Nim sources.
.\" Maintained directly as man(7) source.
.
.TH "AETHER" "1" "November 25, 2026" "aether" "aether Manual"
.
.SH "NAME"
\fBaether\fR \- Aureole policy and workflow controller
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBaether\fR \fIdomain\fR \fIaction\fR [\fIargs\fR\.\.\.]
.br
\fBaether layout bias\fR [\fBleft\fR | \fBright\fR]
.
.P
Commands may be chained with a separate period argument (\fB.\fR).
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBaether\fR is the policy, workflow, geometry, and filesystem helper layer
for Aureole\. It provides higher\-level window, group, layout, rule, and state
operations with explicit window IDs on commands that accept them\.
.
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
Commands have no global option parser or supported help/version switch.
Window IDs, where accepted, use 0x followed by eight hexadecimal digits.
Omitted target IDs default to the focused window.
Grid counts, indices and positions are positive and one-based.
An optional argument in one command does not imply support in other commands.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "DAEMON"
.TP 7
.B daemon await
Wait for the daemon to establish its snapshot baseline and finish initial
refresh processing. Retry an unavailable socket every 100 milliseconds;
there is no overall timeout. Other IPC errors fail immediately.
This command does not launch the daemon.

.
.SS "DISPLAY"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBdisplay height\fR: Print display height\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBdisplay width\fR: Print display width\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBdisplay width_test ge|gt|ne|eq|le|lt WIDTH\fR: Compare display width with
an integer; exit 0 if true, 1 if false. Initial-capital operators such as Ge
are also accepted\.
.
.TP 7
.B display dimensions
Print display width and height separated by a space.
.SS "SCREEN"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen gap\fR: Print the configured gap\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen indent\fR: Print the configured indentation\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen margin\fR: Print the configured margin\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen panel\fR: Print the configured panel height as an integer\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen top\fR: Print the configured top offset\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBscreen bottom\fR: Print the configured bottom offset\.
.
.SS "GROUP"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup add GROUP [WINID]\fR: Record filesystem membership and remembered
focus for the target, defaulting to the focused window. This does not assign
WM membership; use window group for that\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup remove [\-\-close] [WINID]\fR: Remove filesystem membership and
remembered-focus entries for the target, defaulting to the focused window.
With \-\-close, also request closure. This does not itself remove WM
membership\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup close GROUP\fR: Request closure of recorded group members, clear the
WM group, and remove its filesystem membership, focus and deactivation
records\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup count\fR: Print the WM group-slot count, including reserved slot 0\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup current\fR: Print the current WM group from the daemon cache\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup desktop GROUP\fR: Deactivate other public groups, activate the
requested group, and focus its remembered window if still valid\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup focus GROUP\fR: Activate the requested group and focus its valid
remembered window. If already current, record the focused window in that
group\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup id NAME\fR: Print a built-in group-name ID. Names are case-sensitive:
VOID=0, DESK=1, COMM=2, CODE=3, WIKI=4, UTIL=5, PLAY=6, PEER=7\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup last\fR: Focus the public group recorded under $GROUP/last, if
present\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup name [GROUP]\fR: Print the name for an ID, defaulting to the live
current group. This observation accepts reserved ID 0 (VOID); IDs beyond
built-in names print GROUP N\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup reconcile GROUP\fR: Validate a public group argument against the live
WM. The current implementation makes no filesystem or WM changes\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup restore\fR: Activate every public group, clear deactivation records,
and preserve the focused window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBgroup toggle GROUP\fR: Deactivate a populated group, or reactivate one
recorded as deactivated and focus its remembered window\.
.
.P
Public action group IDs are one\-based and less than \fBgroup count\fR; 0 is
reserved VOID. Observation commands may report 0. Numeric group arguments do
not accept built-in names; use \fBgroup id NAME\fR to look up a name.
.
.TP 7
.B group next
Print the next public group ID, wrapping at the public range boundary.
This does not change groups.
.TP 7
.B group previous
Print the previous public group ID, wrapping at the public range boundary.
This does not change groups.
.TP 7
.B group tagcount
Print the number of built-in public group names (7).
.SS "WINDOW"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow await CLASS | \-\-name PATTERN | SECONDS\fR: Wait up to five seconds
for a matching managed class or title, then focus the unique match. Class
matching is exact; title matching uses a case-insensitive regular expression.
Multiple matches fail. A positive numeric argument sleeps for that many
seconds instead. No property argument is supported\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow classname\fR: Print the focused window class\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow count [CLASS | \-\-name PATTERN] [\-\-all]\fR: Count daemon-cached
matching windows; defaults to mapped windows. The group filter is not accepted
here\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow extend DIRECTION [left|right] [WINID]\fR: Extend the target toward
left, right, near, far, top or bottom; the optional side qualifies top or
bottom\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow geometry [WINID]\fR: Print X=, Y=, WIDTH= and HEIGHT= lines for the
explicit or focused window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow group GROUP [\-\-teleport]\fR: Assign the focused window to a public
WM group. With \-\-teleport, also focus a surviving recorded member of the
source group, when available\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow layer\fR \fInormal|above|overlay\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Set a persistent
WM stacking layer without changing focus\. \fBoverlay\fR stays above
\fBabove\fR, which stays above \fBnormal\fR\. The target defaults to the
focused window; normal restores ordinary stacking\. An explicit assignment
overrides EWMH defaults until the managed client is destroyed/unmanaged,
including across hide/remap\. Title\-case layer names remain accepted\. Docks
and EWMH ABOVE windows automatically participate in the WM above tier without
aether or aetherd rules\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow hide\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Hide a window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow ids [CLASS | \-\-name PATTERN] [\-\-all] [\-\-group GROUP]\fR: Print
matching daemon-cached window IDs, one per line. Defaults to mapped windows.
Class matching is exact; title matching uses a case-insensitive regular
expression. The group filter narrows membership without implying \-\-all. Use
either a class or a title selector\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow restore\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Restore saved window geometry\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow rotate\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Swap the selected window's width and
height\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow shift up|down|left|right [WINID]\fR: Move the target by one current
window height or width and save its previous geometry\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow size SIZE [\-\-rotate] [\-\-larger|\-\-smaller] [WINID]\fR: Resize
using WIDTHxHEIGHT, a non-square WIDTH:HEIGHT ratio, or a preset. Presets are
viewport, terminal, paper, video, A3, B4, A4, B5, A5, B6, A6, B7, 480p, 720p,
1080p and 1440p. paper and video require \-\-larger or \-\-smaller. \-\-rotate
swaps the selected dimensions\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow move X Y\fR: Move the focused window by signed relative pixel
offsets. Exactly two arguments are accepted; an explicit window ID is not
accepted\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow snap DIRECTION [AXIS] [WINID]\fR: Position the target at left,
right, near, center, top or bottom. AXIS may be left, right, horizontal or
vertical where applicable (for example center horizontal or top left)\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow spread POSITION [QUALIFIERS] [WINID]\fR: Place the target without
resizing. POSITION is left, right, center, a column number, or COLUMNS COLUMN.
Optional \-\-rows ROWS and \-\-row ROW choose a grid row; top or bottom may
select the row. A lone number selects a column in an automatically sized grid.
With COLUMNS, COLUMN may be numeric, left, right or center\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow stack\fR [\fIwinid\fR]: Print the overlap\-connected stack for a
window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow swap up|down|left|right|north|south|east|west\fR: Focus the adjacent
window in the requested direction and exchange its geometry with the
previously focused window; fail if no adjacent window is found\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow tile left|right|COLUMNS [COLUMN] [\-\-rows ROWS] [\-\-row ROW]
[WINID]\fR: Resize and position the target in the grid (default COLUMN is
COLUMNS; default row count and row are 1). Numeric COLUMN is relative to the
current layout bias: physical column is COLUMN for left bias and
COLUMNS \- COLUMN + 1 for right bias. Physical columns run left to right.
The omitted COLUMN follows the same rule. left or right extends the target
to that literal physical edge and fills the usable height, independently of bias\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow toggle CLASS | \-\-name PATTERN\fR: Find matching windows including
unmapped windows; hide each, or focus it if the hide request fails. Exit 1 if
there are no matches\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow wm\-group\fR \fIwinid\fR: Print the WM\-reported group for an
explicit ID\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow wm\-groups\fR: Print WM groups for managed windows\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBwindow snapshot\fR: Print the normalized WM snapshot\.
.
.P
\fBwm\-group\fR, \fBwm\-groups\fR, and \fBsnapshot\fR are read\-only
observations\. The \fBwindow stack\-geometries\fR and \fBwindow
apply\-geometries\fR commands are Borealis commands; they are not aether
public actions\.
.
.SS "LAYOUT"
.
The \fBlayout\fR and \fBlayouts\fR domains are interchangeable\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayout bias [left | right]\fR: Query or set the global horizontal placement
preference used by all numeric tile operations and applicable layout assignment
policies\. Without an argument, print the current bias (\fBleft\fR or
\fBright\fR)\. \fBleft\fR preserves the established assignment preference;
\fBright\fR mirrors it horizontally\.
The default is \fBleft\fR\. Setting bias does not reposition existing windows
or invoke a layout operation\. Invalid arguments are rejected without changing
the current bias\.
.
.P
A running \fBaetherd\fR is required to query or set bias\. The daemon maintains
bias across independent \fBaether\fR invocations for its lifetime\.
Restarting \fBaetherd\fR resets bias to \fBleft\fR\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts explode\fR: Capture the current overlap\-connected stack, save
original geometry, and arrange those windows according to the existing layout
rule and current bias\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts unexplode\fR: Restore saved geometry for surviving exploded
windows\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts explode \-\-group\fR \fIgroup\fR: Place visible group members using
the fold grid engine with the current bias and save a dedicated
identity\-bearing explode operation under \fB$WME/layout/explode:group:N\fR\.
Each group retains independent state\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts unexplode \-\-group\fR \fIgroup\fR: Restore that recorded
operation, including surviving clients that changed groups or became hidden\.
New members and reused XIDs with different identity tokens are not restored\.
Preserve current focus and remove the saved operation after restoration\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts fold COLUMNS [CLASS | \-\-group GROUP] [\-\-rows ROWS] [\-\-spread]
[\-\-record]\fR: Fold matching mapped windows into a grid using the current
bias (ROWS defaults to 1; \-\-spread preserves window sizes), then raise
participants in placement order
within their effective stacking bands while preserving focus\. Repeating an
unchanged fold still raises the selected set\. Group explode shares this
stacking behavior without sharing fold transaction ownership\. Add
\fB\-\-record\fR to create or extend a persistent checkpoint for the selected
class, group, or all visible windows\. Without it, fold only arranges
windows\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts unfold\fR [\fIclass\fR | \fB\-\-group\fR \fIgroup\fR]: Restore and
consume the matching recorded class or group checkpoint\. With no selector,
restore the checkpoint created by a recorded selector\-less fold\. Each scope
preserves the first geometry per (winid, ClientToken) and adds newly
encountered identities on later recorded folds; clients appearing after the
last recorded fold are not included\. Restoration preserves current focus and
does not restore stacking order or persistent layers\. Class names with path
separators are percent\-encoded in the state directory name\. Ordinary fold
history remains available independently\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts level\fR: Center mapped windows vertically\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts restore [\-\-all]\fR: Restore window geometry history for mapped
clients, or all clients with \-\-all, preserving focus\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts spread COLUMNS [COLUMN] [\-\-rows ROWS] [\-\-position POSITION]
[WINID]\fR: Place one target without resizing, using layout grid placement
order with the current bias. Rows and position default to 1; COLUMN overrides
the column derived from POSITION\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBlayouts tile COLUMNS [COLUMN] [\-\-rows ROWS] [\-\-position POSITION]
[WINID]\fR: Resize and position one target using layout grid placement order
with the current bias.
Rows and position default to 1. Explicit numeric COLUMN is bias-relative:
physical column is COLUMN for left bias and COLUMNS \- COLUMN + 1 for right
bias. Without COLUMN, POSITION selects the established assignment order,
mirrored horizontally for right bias exactly once. Rows, sizes and vertical
positions are independent of bias\.
.
.P
Numeric tile semantics also apply to fluent window operations and resident
application rules; rules require no individual bias handling. Each numeric
tile operation captures the authoritative bias once. Resident policy reads
Aetherd state directly; remote commands query Aetherd. Later preference changes
affect subsequent operations. Low-level physical grid placement receives
resolved physical columns and performs no bias lookup or transformation.
Explicit cardinal left and right operations remain physical. CENTER_BIAS is
an independent centering preference\.
.
.P
\fBunexplode\fR ignores disappeared saved XIDs and preserves the current
focus\.
.
.TP 7
.B layouts grid COLUMNS [CLASS | \-\-group GROUP] [\-\-rows ROWS]
Print an adjusted grid as COLUMNS \-\-rows ROWS for the selected mapped
windows.
Fail if there are no matches. Does not arrange windows.
.P
For layouts tile and layouts spread, no more than six arguments may follow
the action name (each option name and value counts separately).
Thus COLUMN, rows, position and WINID cannot all be supplied together.
.SS "RULE"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBrule NAME\fR: Apply a built-in application rule to the focused managed
window. No additional arguments are accepted\.
.
.P
Supported rule names are:
aerc, asunder, audacious, btop, calibre, cbftp, chromium, Chromium,
compose, darktable, email, feh, firefox, foliate, fontmatrix, gftp, gimp,
halloy, kak, krita, luakit, manpage, mpv, music, nicotine, oculante,
palette, pavucontrol, pcmanfm, qutebrowser, qutebrowser-whoops,
rapidraw, rawtherapee, surf, term, tmux, wiki, xftp, yazi, yazi-root,
youtube and zathura. Names are case-sensitive; rules are compiled in.
.SS "STATE"
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBstate snapshot [WINID]\fR: Save geometry and client identity under
$WME/snapshot/WINID, defaulting to the focused window\.
.
.IP "\(bu" 4
\fBstate restore [WINID]\fR: Copy the saved snapshot into $WINFO/WINID after
validating client identity. This updates geometry history; it does not apply
geometry to the window. Use window restore afterwards to apply it\.
.
.P
\fBaetherd\fR removes \fB$WINFO/<winid>\fR after receiving an actual X11
\fBDestroyNotify\fR and confirming that the window no longer exists\. Hidden,
unmapped, and inactive\-group windows retain their state\. Startup and X11
reconnection also reconcile stale WINFO directories, including windows that
died while the daemon was stopped\. Uncertain X11 errors preserve state\.
.
.P
The same lifecycle handler reconciles \fB$HIDDEN/<winid>\fR on \fBMapNotify\fR
and \fBDestroyNotify\fR, checking current X visibility before removing an
entry\. Visible or destroyed windows lose hidden metadata; genuinely unmapped
windows retain it\. Startup/reconnection scans both trees, including hidden
entries without WINFO records\. No particular focus or restore command is
required\.
.
.P
WINFO cleanup waits for active restore\-history transactions and retries
deferred work; HIDDEN cleanup proceeds independently\. Group membership and
focus records remain owned by WM snapshot reconciliation\. Correctness does
not require an explicit \fBaether group close\fR before closing an
application\.
.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT AND FILES"
Use the environment established by the intended CaelWM session.
The controller does not load a configuration file on invocation.
.TP 7
.B DISPLAY, XAUTHORITY
Select and authorize the X11 connection.
.TP 7
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
When nonempty, daemon IPC uses $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/zephyr/zephyrd.sock.
The legacy names are intentional compatibility paths.
.TP 7
.B WME
Runtime state root: layout checkpoints are under $WME/layout,
explicit snapshots under $WME/snapshot, and the daemon-published WM snapshot
is $WME/wm/snapshot. If XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is empty, the IPC socket is
$WME/zephyrd.sock. At least one socket-root variable must be set for IPC.
.TP 7
.B WINFO
Per-window geometry history and identity records, under $WINFO/WINID.
.TP 7
.B GROUP
Filesystem group mirror, with related roots $GROUP:focus and
$GROUP:deactivated; $GROUP/current and $GROUP/last track selection history.
.TP 7
.B HIDDEN
Per-window hidden metadata, under $HIDDEN/WINID.
.TP 7
.B WMSE
Session settings tree. Screen metrics are read from $WMSE/ui and
$WMSE/panel directory names and their numeric child directories.
.TP 7
.B CENTER_BIAS
For spread placement with an even column count, choose left or right
(default right) as the center column.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Successful commands normally return 0. Invalid commands, invalid arguments,
daemon errors and failed predicates return nonzero (normally 1).
With no arguments, usage is printed and the process exits 1.
.SH "CHAINING"
Commands can be sequenced with a separate period argument. They run in order;
a failing command stops the chain. display width_test terminates the entire
invocation with its predicate status, even on success. window size terminal
also terminates the invocation after applying its saved terminal size.
Each command resolves
its own target:
.
.IP "" 4
.
.nf

aether window move 10 10 . window size 800x600
.
.fi
.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
aether daemon await
aether group focus "$(aether group next)"
aether window ids \-\-all \-\-group 3
aether layouts fold 3 \-\-group 3 \-\-record
aether layouts unfold \-\-group 3
aether state snapshot 0x01234567
aether state restore 0x01234567 . window restore 0x01234567
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBborealis\fR(1), \fBaureole\fR(1), \fBaetherd\fR(1)
